## Required Context Files

**Lost or unsure what to do? Read `$AGENT_OS_SOURCE/START_HERE.md` first** — operator decision tree and recovery guide (thin-client; no local `.ai/`).

**Free-text entry:** don't know which skill to run? Invoke `@ai-director - <what you want>` (Agent OS), `@ui-director` (`.ai.ui`), `@biz-director` (`.ai.biz`), `@soc-director` (`.ai.soc`), or `@x-director` for cross-framework work.

### Frameworks registry (cross-framework discovery)

Sister frameworks are siblings on disk; `.ai/` is the Agent OS source. Paths resolve at runtime.

| Framework | Director | Path | Bootstrap artifact |
|-----------|----------|------|--------------------|
| `.ai` (Agent OS) | `@ai-director` | *source via AGENT_OS_SOURCE* | `skills/README.md` |
| `.ai.ui` (UI Design OS) | `@ui-director` | `/mnt/work/Projects/.ai.ui` | `.ai.ui/skills/README.md` |
| `.ai.biz` (Business OS) | `@biz-director` | `/mnt/work/Projects/.ai.biz` | `.ai.biz/skills/README.md` |
| `.ai.soc` (Social OS) | `@soc-director` | `/mnt/work/Projects/.ai.soc` | `.ai.soc/skills/README.md` |

**Path resolution:** (1) use a filled path cell; empty → fall through. (2) Auto-discover: thin-client parent = `$AGENT_OS_SOURCE/..`; check `${parent}/.ai.ui|.ai.biz|.ai.soc`; missing = "not installed". (3) Before routing, verify the framework dir + its `skills/README.md` exist; if absent, route to `@ai-director` prefixed `[degraded: <framework> not installed]` — never route into the void.

### Source resolution (thin-client — mandatory before any `.ai/...` path)

AGENT_OS_SOURCE=/mnt/work/Projects/.ai

| Variable | Value |
|----------|-------|
| `AGENT_OS_SOURCE` | `/mnt/work/Projects/.ai` |
| `AI_UI_SOURCE` | `/mnt/work/Projects/.ai.ui` |

**Rules:**
1. `.cursorrules` + `.work/**` + `.work.ui/**` — always local.
2. Every `.ai/<path>` or `.ai.ui/<path>` resolves from the matching source above (skills, standards, concepts, scripts, templates).
3. If a source path is unreadable → stop and report `agent-os source unreachable` or `ui-design-os source unreachable` — do not guess.
4. Gate scripts use pre-resolved absolute paths in § Change safety (do not re-derive).

