## Workflow Rules

### Planning
- Plans live under `.work/plans/` (foundation, full plan, registries, operations runbooks).
- Wait for approval before large code changes when the user asked for a plan only.
- Ask for confirmation before applying edits when scope is unclear.

### Deletion
- NEVER delete files without explicit user permission.

### Git
- NEVER execute `git commit` or `git push` unless the user explicitly requests it in the same message.
- **`@session-control close commit` / `close commit push` / `commit` / `commit push` (mandatory):** When the user invokes session-control with **`commit`** (and optional **`push`**), you **MUST** run shell `git add` + `git commit` per `.ai/skills/session-control/skill.md` — stage all **safe** dirty paths (default scope), not HANDOFF/NEXT only. If **`push`** was requested, run `git push` after a successful commit. Show `git log -1 --oneline` and `git status -sb`; do not claim commit succeeded without a commit SHA when the tree was dirty. Standalone `commit`/`commit push` do not update HANDOFF or NEXT.
- Otherwise provide commit commands for the user when they will commit themselves.
- Never add `Co-authored-by:` trailers. Install hooks once: `bash /mnt/work/Projects/.ai/scripts/install-git-hooks.sh`.
- Never modify git history (rebase, force-push) without explicit user request.

### No Attribution / No Signatures
- Do NOT add "Generated by", "Created by", dates, or agent signatures to files you create or modify.
- The user is the sole responsible party.

---

## Verification & Communication

- Before "complete": run applicable tests/lint/type; report actual output (see Core Principles §2–3, §7).
- On failure: report exact error, diagnose, fix, re-run.
- Scope: declare scope first (§ Change safety); be concise; label uncertainty.

---

## External Documentation

- Use **Context7 MCP** (`@upstash/context7-mcp`) for version-specific library docs when configured.
- Otherwise use web search to verify current APIs before writing integration code.

---

## Commit Message Format (When Providing to User)

- Plain text only — NO surrounding quotes, NO parentheses wrapping the message.
- Format: `type: short description` followed by optional blank line and body.
- Valid types: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `docs`, `chore`, `style`, `test`.
- Example (correct): `fix: handle empty payload on webhook retry`
- Example (wrong): `"fix(webhook): empty payload"`

